# Tarballs live in R2 (dl.kama-lang.org), never in this tree. Rules are tried in order and a redirect beats a
# static file, so the first rule keeps every index.json served from here, the second sends a package page's
# explicit `index.html` to the page itself, and the third sends everything else below a package — its tarballs —
# to the bucket. The page at `/@kama/<pkg>/` needs no rule: a placeholder matches no empty segment (measured with
# `wrangler pages dev`, 2026-10-02). tools/check.py requires exactly these three rules, in order.
/@kama/:pkg/index.json /@kama/:pkg/index.json 200
/@kama/:pkg/index.html /@kama/:pkg/ 301
/@kama/:pkg/:file https://dl.kama-lang.org/@kama/:pkg/:file 302
